    "type": "question",
    "label": null,
    "prompt": "Priya collects 20c and 50c coins in a money box. The box contains five more 20c coins than 50c coins.\nAltogether there is \\$8.00 in the box.\nForm and solve an equation to find the number, $x$, of 50c coins in the box.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$20(x+5)+50x=800$; $x=10$. There are 10 fifty-cent coins.",
      "worked": "Let $x$ be the number of 50c coins.\nNumber of 20c coins $=x+5$\nUsing cents:\n$$\\begin{align*}20(x+5)+50x&=800\\\\70x+100&=800\\\\70x&=700\\\\x&=10\\end{align*}$$\nThere are 10 fifty-cent coins and 15 twenty-cent coins.\nCheck: $20(15)+50(10)=800$ cents, or \\$8.00.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": null
  },
